# The canonical sitemap path.
#
# @astrojs/sitemap writes sitemap-index.xml for a site with any routes, and
# the old /sitemap.xml path 404s. Search engines and crawlers commonly request
# /sitemap.xml first, so that request was answering 404 for every crawler that
# tried it. One rule fixes it without a second sitemap file.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301

# The legacy paths that answer a search but no longer exist.
